P-5: spec 004's amendments to the arrival check (tasks.md T036; contracts/intake-amendments.md §7; FR-015, FR-023,
FR-077 items 3 and 4). Made on feat/004-intake against main a964494 (P-1 to P-4 applied); apply after M8, then the
P-6 commit, P-7, and P-8 (docs/merge-requests/2026-10-27-feat-004-intake.md). git apply skips this header.

    BEFORE YOU APPLY IT: the Author confirms or replaces this term before applying P-5 (T031).

    MARK_HUMAN, the mark of a file whose record's steps are all by hand, is the plan's candidate, digitalCreation,
    unverified (research R-53). The patch adds it as one line of tools/gates/arrival_check.py:

        +MARK_HUMAN = "digitalCreation"

    If IPTC's term for media a person made with digital tools differs, that line takes it, and nothing else in the
    patch changes (the tests read the term from the check). It is an added line, so the hunk still applies after
    the edit. The note gives the edit, and the scrubber's matching line.

It changes three files:
- tools/gates/arrival_check.py: M5 (C1, the mark the record's steps call for, and trainedAlgorithmicMedia alone
  under assets/twin/ and docs/research/images/), R1 (C2, design), P2 (C4, screens_plain_live_face, true or
  not_applicable), P1 (C1, main's approval of the hash of any file whose record's steps call for a mark but
  trainedAlgorithmicMedia, wherever it lives; C5, likeness_accepted not_applicable for a room file with no likeness),
  F3 (C6, every room file at gzip-9, phase 3 once assets/room/ holds one), F2 (C7, per_asset.room's six keys, exit 2
  otherwise), and AMENDMENTS = ("004-C1", "004-C2", "004-C4", "004-C5", "004-C6", "004-C7").
- tools/gates/test/test_arrival_check.py and tools/gates/test/arrival_fixtures.py: §7's cases, built at run time.
  Spec 003's R7 case, whose visitors' still mixes a model step and a hand step, gets main's approval of its hash.

Regenerated after T041's review (part 1, I1 and nit 5): the P1 clause above, and its tests; a non-room kind under
assets/room/ is tested against P1, P2, and F2.

